{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01MPbnRWZzFhH5z1Aqmk65Vk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I need to produce the planning artifacts:\n\n1. `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-c69/20260505T005214Z-QuantAgent-c69-planner/result.json` - Result summary\n2. `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-c69/20260505T005214Z-QuantAgent-c69-planner/run-report.md` - Run report\n3. `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-c69/20260505T005214Z-QuantAgent-c69-planner/commands.log` - Commands run\n\n\n4. `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-c69/20260505T005214Z-QuantAgent-c69-planner/quality-gates.log` - Quality gates\n\nAnd the actual planning docs under the docs/ directory:\n- `docs/02_planning/QuantAgent-c69-PL-llm-agent-strategy-m1.md` - Planning document\n- `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-c69-AC-llm-agent-strategy.md` - Acceptance criteria\n- `docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-c69-IM-llm-agent-strategy.md` - Implementation guide\n\nI also need to update the README files in those directories to reference the new docs. Now I'm thinking through what the planning document should cover — the M1 strategy itself, the current state of the codebase with the existing `LLMAgentStrategy` wrapper and `TradingGraph` orchestrator, what needs to be implemented from both the implementer and tester perspective, the concrete steps to take, and how to validate everything with a reference backtest.\n\nLooking at the codebase, I can see the multi-agent pipeline is already in place with the graph setup, shared state management, and backtest engine integration. The unit tests cover signal parsing and graph invocation well, but there's a documentation gap — the strategy exists and works but isn't documented as a first-class reference, there's no minimal config profile for running an end-to-end backtest, and the integration testing could be more comprehensive.\n\nI'm also noticing a potential schema mismatch: the `LLMAgentStrategy` expects `reasoning` and `decision_report` fields from the graph output, but these aren't defined in the `IndicatorAgentState` TypedDict, which suggests the decision agent is outputting extra fields that fall outside the state schema. I need to verify whether the `reasoning` field is consistently populated from the graph and properly mapped to the signal's `analysis_summary`.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":474,"cache_read_input_tokens":59803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":474},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce2496a8-a497-4f7a-9d36-07ca768dd87e","uuid":"3e3fea3c-1bcd-4c06-988e-e9f1f2246e50"}
